        "chinese": "这是新手错觉。Reviewer看到全面诚实之局限, 反而上调对paper之信任。隐藏局限才是真弱点, 因为reviewer会自己找, 然后reject。古典文学领域尤其如此, 文献历来散佚, 不acknowledge = 不专业。",
        "pinyin": "Zhè shì xīnshǒu cuòjué. Reviewer kàn dào quánmiàn chéngshí zhī júxiàn, fǎn'ér shàngdiào duì paper zhī xìnrèn. Yǐncáng júxiàn cái shì zhēn ruòdiǎn, yīnwèi reviewer huì zìjǐ zhǎo, ránhòu reject. Gǔdiǎn wénxué lǐngyù yóuqí rúcǐ, wénxiàn lìlái sànyì, bù acknowledge = bù zhuānyè.",
        "english": "Beginner's illusion. Reviewers seeing comprehensive, honest limitations actually upgrade their trust. Hiding limitations is the real weakness — reviewers will find them and reject. Especially in classical literature, where documents have always been scattered — not acknowledging = unprofessional.",
