    "register_notes": "Hedging trong phê bình văn học C2 đòi hỏi tinh tế hơn academic discourse C1: thêm 文白 hedges (殆 / 庶几 / 恐) + reception aesthetics awareness + textual scholarship caution.\n\n1. THREE-LAYER HEDGING — LITERARY VERSION:\n\nLAYER 1 — REPORT FACT (most flexible):\n- 据现存文献 (according to extant documents)\n- 就笔者所见 (as far as the author has seen)\n- 目前可考者 (those examinable at present)\n- 在A本中 (in edition A)\nNeutral, low risk. C2 must replace simple statements with these hedges.\n\nLAYER 2 — EXPLAIN MECHANISM:\n- 似乎 (seems)\n- 或可 (perhaps may)\n- 在某种程度上 (to some extent)\n- 殆 (probably — 文白)\n- 庶几 (perhaps approaches — 文白)\n- 恐 (I fear / probably — 文白)\nMedium hedge. C2 favors 文白 markers (殆/庶几/恐) over modern hedges.\n\nLAYER 3 — EXTRAPOLATE / DERIVE:\n- 有待新文献之发现 (awaits discovery of new documents)\n- 尚不足以一概而论 (insufficient for general claim)\n- 远未达定论之阶段 (far from definitive)\n- 不宜过度推衍 (should not over-extrapolate)\n- 当俟后人裁断 (awaits posterity's judgment — 文言 escape hatch)\nStrong hedge. Required for any speculation about historical reception, authorial intent, etc.\n\n2. TEXTUAL SCHOLARSHIP HEDGES:\n\n- 文献散佚率 (document loss rate) — must acknowledge for pre-modern texts\n- 版本流变 (textual transmission variants)\n- 真伪存疑 (authenticity in question)\n- 系年待考 (dating awaits investigation)\n- 题署存疑 (attribution in question)\n\nC2 cần explicit awareness của these issues khi cite 古典.\n\n3. CỤM 不无 (DOUBLE NEGATIVE FORMAL):\n\n- 不无道理 (not without reason)\n- 不无可能 (not without possibility)\n- 不无启发 (not without inspiration)\n- 不无遗憾 (not without regret)\n- 不无益处 (not without benefit)\n\nCực formal. Dùng để hedge rất nhẹ + acknowledge tinh tế. C2 should use 2-3 per essay.\n\n4. SCALE-CALIBRATION FOR LITERARY CLAIMS:\n\nKhi describing impact / reception / popularity:\n\nWEAK CLAIM (safe):\n- 略具影响 (slight influence)\n- 颇有反响 (some resonance)\n- 部分接受 (partial acceptance)\n- 在士人圈中 (within literati circles)\n\nMEDIUM:\n- 影响深远 (deep and lasting influence) — only with strong evidence\n- 广为流传 (widely transmitted) — needs evidence of multiple regions\n- 蔚为大观 (forms a grand sight) — only for established phenomenon\n\nSTRONG (rare, dangerous):\n- 风行海内 (sweeps within seas) — only for clearly documented phenomena\n- 家喻户晓 (household-known) — almost never justified for pre-modern texts\n- 妇孺皆知 (known to women and children) — almost never justified\n\nC2 essay typically stays within WEAK and MEDIUM. Use STRONG only with clear documentary support.\n\n5. UNCERTAINTY MARKERS LEVEL:\n\nUNCERTAINTY HIGH (standard for pre-modern reception):\n- 该现象之机制目前尚不明朗\n- 学界对此存在较大分歧\n- 现有文献不足以得出明确结论\n- 后续发现或将改写本论\n\nUNCERTAINTY MEDIUM:\n- 似乎 / 殆 / 或可\n- 在某种程度上 / 一定条件下\n- 颇有可能 / 不无可能\n\nUNCERTAINTY LOW (claim mạnh — chỉ when 文献 confirms):\n- 文献明载 (documents clearly record)\n- 多家著录均见 (multiple sources record)\n- 已为学界所公认 (already acknowledged by scholarship)\n\n6. NULL / NEGATIVE EVIDENCE TREATMENT:\n\nKhi không tìm thấy reference:\n- '无据可查' (no evidence to investigate)\n- '于现存文献中未见' (not seen in extant documents)\n- '此说目前尚乏佐证' (this view currently lacks corroboration)\n\nKhông được viết 'X 不存在' (X did not exist) — chỉ '于现存文献中未见X' (not seen in extant documents).\n\nThis is critical distinction. Absence of evidence ≠ evidence of absence — sinh viên Việt thường mismatch.\n\n7. TRANSLATING ENGLISH HEDGES:\n\nEnglish 'arguably' → 或可言之 / 似可\nEnglish 'tentatively' → 暂时 / 初步而言\nEnglish 'plausibly' → 似不无可能 / 殆\nEnglish 'apparently' → 显然 (rare; usually 似乎)\nEnglish 'putatively' → 据传 / 一般认为\n\n不要 directly translate 'I think' → 我认为 (口语). Use 笔者以为 / 笔者愚以为.\n\n8. SCHOLAR-DEFERENCE HEDGES:\n\n- 笔者愚以为 (this humble author thinks)\n- 学生愚见 (this student's humble view)\n- 不揣冒昧 (without weighing presumption)\n- 拙文中... (in this clumsy article)\n- 谨向先生请益 (humbly requesting your guidance)\n\nC2 essay typically opens with 1-2 humble markers, especially when contradicting senior.",
