    "register_notes": "Định nghĩa concepts 古典文论 đòi hỏi cả ba kỹ năng: (a) Aristotelian structure, (b) lineage tracing across dynasties, (c) disambiguation từ similar-looking modern terms.\n\n1. ARISTOTELIAN STRUCTURE FOR 古典 CONCEPTS:\n\nGenus (lớp lớn) + Differentia (đặc trưng phân biệt).\n\nVí dụ:\n- 意境 = (genus: 古典诗学审美范畴) + (differentia: 由主体意与客体境互融而成之整体).\n- 风骨 = (genus: 古典文论范畴) + (differentia: 文章之气势与骨力).\n- 神韵 = (genus: 王士禛诗学范畴) + (differentia: 诗境之超逸含蓄).\n\nMột định nghĩa thiếu genus = không khung được. Thiếu differentia = không phân biệt được với cùng-genus terms.\n\n2. LINEAGE TRACING (家谱式追踪):\n\n古典 concepts thường evolve qua nhiều dynasties. C2 essay phải show genealogy:\n- 起源 (origin) — first major use\n- 发展 (development) — successive elaborations\n- 变形 (transformation) — modern reinterpretation\n\nVí dụ '意境':\n- 唐代王昌龄《诗格》(starting point)\n- 严羽《沧浪诗话》(发挥)\n- 明清诗话 (普及)\n- 王国维《人间词话》(转化为'境界')\n\nMỗi station phải có specific text + page/section. Vague genealogy = academic disgrace.\n\n3. DISAMBIGUATION FROM MODERN TERMS:\n\n古典 concepts have modern English approximations đôi khi misleading.\n\n- 意境 ≠ 'mood' (mood is psychological; 意境 is aesthetic-ontological)\n- 气韵 ≠ 'rhythm' (气韵 is spirit-energy resonance, structural-ontological)\n- 风骨 ≠ 'style' (style is generic; 风骨 is moral-aesthetic vigor)\n- 比兴 ≠ 'metaphor' (比 ≈ metaphor, but 兴 is non-equivalent — evocative beginning)\n\nC2 essay phải explicitly call out non-equivalence khi using English term.\n\n4. CỤM TỪ ĐỊNH NGHĨA CHUẨN:\n\n- 所谓 X, 即指 / 是指 (the so-called X refers to)\n- X 一词可定义为 (the term X can be defined as)\n- 笔者拟将 X 界定为 (the author proposes to define X as)\n- 在本文语境下, X 特指 (in this article's context, X specifically refers to)\n- X 之内涵 (the connotation of X)\n- X 之外延 (the extension of X)\n- X 一词原指..., 后引申为... (originally meant..., later extended to...)\n- X 之要义 (the essential meaning of X)\n\n5. HISTORICAL DEVELOPMENT VOCABULARY:\n\n- 滥觞于 (originating from)\n- 发轫于 (starting from)\n- 发挥于 (developed by)\n- 转化为 (transformed into)\n- 沿用至今 (used to this day)\n- 嬗变 (gradual change)\n- 流变 (transmission and evolution)\n- 一脉相承 (continuous lineage)\n\n6. CỤM 顾名思义 (BORDERED USE):\n\n- 'X, 顾名思义, 即指 [short gloss]' — only for terms whose meaning is largely transparent.\n- DON'T use '顾名思义' followed by formal definition. Save for short glosses.\n- For real definitions, use '所谓 X, 即指...'.\n\n7. INTENSION (内涵) vs EXTENSION (外延):\n\n- 内涵 (intension) = essential properties.\n- 外延 (extension) = scope of objects.\n\n古典 critical concepts often have unstable extensions (e.g., '意境' applies to which texts?). C2 essay should show awareness.\n\n8. HANDLING OVERLAPPING CONCEPTS:\n\nSeven concepts overlap heavily in 古典文论: 意境 / 境界 / 神韵 / 气韵 / 风骨 / 兴趣 / 余味. C2 essay must:\n- Explicitly state which concepts you're discussing\n- Define each separately\n- Articulate distinctions: '意境 偏 主客 互融, 神韵 偏 含蓄 超 逸, 二者 形似 神 异'\n- Cite specific source for each definition\n\n9. AVOIDING TRAP: SINGLE-AUTHORITY DEFINITION:\n\nDon't define '意境' solely as Wang Guowei used it — that conflates with 境界 và misrepresents Tang/Song origin. Multi-source definition shows scholarship range.\n\n10. CONTEMPORARY CRITICAL LEXICON:\n\nMixed with 古典 terms, sometimes appropriate:\n- 叙述者 (narrator)\n- 视点 (point of view)\n- 互文性 (intertextuality)\n- 自由间接引语 (free indirect discourse)\n- 接受美学 (reception aesthetics)\n- 副文本 (paratext)\n\nApply to modern texts. Apply to 古典 texts only with explicit hedging acknowledgment of anachronism.",
