    "register_notes": "Đánh giá một nghiên cứu dịch thuật văn học C2 yêu cầu kết hợp critique skill (similar to academic discourse C1) + translation studies awareness + classical-text textual scholarship.\n\n1. CẤU TRÚC CRITIQUE CHUẨN (5 BƯỚC) — same as academic discourse but enriched:\n\n- BƯỚC 1 — ACKNOWLEDGE: '该研究在X方面有价值'.\n- BƯỚC 2 — TRANSITION: '然而 / 然 / 不过'.\n- BƯỚC 3 — IDENTIFY ISSUES: numbered (其一 / 其二 / 其三).\n- BƯỚC 4 — SUGGEST SOLUTIONS: '笔者建议 / 或可考虑'.\n- BƯỚC 5 — OVERALL ASSESSMENT: '瑕不掩瑜 + recommend' / '尚不足以 + recommend reject'.\n\n2. SOFTNESS GRADUATION FOR LITERARY TRANSLATION CRITIQUE:\n\nLIGHT critique:\n- 略显不足 / 美中不足 / 尚有改进空间 / 似可商榷\n\nMEDIUM critique:\n- 存在若干问题 / 论据略嫌薄弱 / 此论恐难成立 / 有待商榷 / 略显简化\n\nHEAVY critique (rare):\n- 论证存在严重缺陷 / 此论实属误解 / 实属时代错置\n\n3. TYPES OF TRANSLATION-STUDIES METHODOLOGY ISSUES:\n\nA. SOURCE-TEXT TREATMENT: which edition? does paper acknowledge multiple editions of original?\nB. TARGET-TEXT SELECTION: which translations? how were they chosen? temporal range?\nC. THEORETICAL FRAMEWORK: Mounin (1960s) vs Toury (1990s) vs cultural turn (Bassnett-Lefevere 1990s) vs descriptive (Even-Zohar polysystem).\nD. UNIT OF ANALYSIS: individual words, phrases, lines, stanzas, whole poem?\nE. EVALUATION CRITERIA: form-fidelity? meaning-fidelity? aesthetic-effect? reader-response?\nF. GENERALIZABILITY: single text → entire corpus? Single translator → all translators?\n\n4. SPECIFIC TRANSLATION-CRITIQUE PHRASES:\n\n- 形似 vs 神似 (formal-likeness vs spiritual-likeness — 傅雷)\n- 信达雅 (faithfulness, expressiveness, elegance — 严复 1898)\n- 译者主体性 (translator's subjectivity)\n- 翻译伦理 (translation ethics)\n- 文化亏损 (cultural loss)\n- 文化补偿 (cultural compensation)\n- 异化 vs 归化 (foreignization vs domestication — Venuti)\n- 可译性 (translatability)\n- 不可译性 (untranslatability)\n\n5. CỤM PHẢN BIỆN CỤ THỂ:\n\n- 此论尚需斟酌 (this point needs deliberation)\n- 笔者持保留意见 (the author maintains reservations)\n- 论据不足以支撑该结论 (evidence insufficient for the conclusion)\n- 该结论之外推性需谨慎 (extrapolation needs caution)\n- 翻译评价 标准 之 不 透 明 (opacity of evaluation criteria)\n- 历 史 语 境 论 述 之 缺 失 (absence of historical-context discussion)\n\n6. CONSTRUCTIVE SUGGESTIONS:\n\n- 建议 补 充 X 实 验 / X 案 例\n- 或可考虑 + alternative method (could consider...)\n- 宜在 X 部分 增加 论述\n- 数据 / 案例 宜 进一步 细化\n- 框架 宜 升 级 至 contemporary translation studies\n\n7. CLASSIC TRANSLATION-STUDIES CRITIQUE TARGETS:\n\n- Single-translator focus (ignore translator network)\n- Form/meaning binary (ignore cultural turn)\n- Source-text only (ignore target-system polysystem)\n- Lack of historical-context\n- Over-claim generalizability\n- Missing translation-criticism framework (Berman, Toury, Even-Zohar)\n\n8. REVIEW DECISION:\n\n- 接受 (accept) — minor revision only\n- 修改后接受 (accept after revision) — minor revision\n- 重大修改 (major revision) — substantive issues, paper has potential\n- 拒稿 (reject) — fundamental flaws, can resubmit\n- 拒稿不予再审 (reject, no resubmission) — extreme cases\n\n9. CRITIQUE-SPECIFIC IDIOMS:\n\n- 瑕不掩瑜 — flaws don't hide gems (positive evaluation despite issues)\n- 美中不足 — minor flaw in beauty (mostly positive)\n- 见仁见智 — matter of opinion (matters of legitimate disagreement)\n- 一叶障目 — leaf blocks view (singular focus missing big picture)\n- 力所不逮 — force doesn't reach (acknowledging limits)\n- 大相径庭 — vastly different (used when noting discrepancy)\n\n10. CULTURAL CAUTIONS:\n\n- KHÔNG attack translator personally. Critique theory / framework / specific choices.\n- KHÔNG criticize 民族 / 文化. Focus on textual / methodological.\n- ACKNOWLEDGE translator as equal — even if critique is sharp.\n- DOUBLE-BLIND review preserves face. Single-blind requires extra cultural sensitivity (you may know the translator).",
