    "register_notes": "Viết abstract trong phê bình văn học C2 đòi hỏi kỹ năng signature. Sinh viên với bài thí nghiệm xuất sắc cũng có thể bị reject vì abstract yếu.\n\n1. ABSTRACT 4-ELEMENT STRUCTURE (200-300 words):\n\nFORMAT chuẩn:\n- Câu 1-2 (RESEARCH QUESTION + GAP): không 近年来 mở đầu! Trực tiếp: '本文采[方法]重读[文本], 探讨[问题]'.\n- Câu 3 (CONTRIBUTION): '本文提出[name], 通过[mechanism]实现[capability]'.\n- Câu 4-5 (METHOD + CASE): mô tả ngắn cách method hoạt động + textual case range.\n- Câu 6-7 (FINDINGS): 'reading 表明 + 量化数字 / qualitative finding'. AT LEAST 2 specific findings.\n- Câu 8 (CONCLUSION + IMPLICATION): '综上, X 为 Y 提供了 Z'.\n\n2. AVOID PHRASES (kill rate cao):\n\n- '近年来, 随着X的迅猛发展...' — banned.\n- '本文研究了一个非常重要的问题' — vô nghĩa.\n- '具有重要的理论意义和实践价值' — empty.\n- '希望本研究能为该领域做出贡献' — humble nhưng nội dung trống.\n\n3. INFORMATION DENSITY TEST:\n\nĐọc lại từng câu trong abstract. Hỏi: 'nếu xóa câu này, abstract có còn đứng vững không?'.\n- KHÔNG = câu cần thiết, giữ.\n- CÓ = câu vô ích, xóa.\n\nMục tiêu: 100% câu pass test này.\n\n4. NUMBERS & SPECIFICS:\n\nMỗi abstract phải có ít nhất 2 specific details:\n- Chapter range: '《红楼梦》第27至32回'\n- Translation comparison: 'Hawkes 与 杨戴 之译本'\n- Time period: '明嘉靖至万历, 即1522-1620'\n- Edition: '中华书局1979年点校本'\n- Quantitative: '在 全书 共 81 难 中, 第 X 难 至 第 Y 难 之间'\n\nSpecifics convince, không phải adjectives.\n\n5. LITERATURE REVIEW NGUYÊN TẮC:\n\nTRÁNH (堆砌):\n- 'X et al. did Y. Then Z et al. did W. Then ...': chronological listing.\n- Tóm tắt mỗi paper 1 câu: không có analysis.\n\nSHOULD (提纲挈领):\n- Identify 2-4 'schools' hoặc 'approaches' trong field.\n- Show progression: foundational → mainstream → recent advances.\n- Identify gaps / open problems.\n- Position your work explicitly: '本研究填补了 X gap'.\n\n6. CỤM TỪ STRUCTURE LIT REVIEW:\n\n- 该领域之研究大致可分为三类 (the field's research roughly divides into three categories)\n- 早期工作 (early work)... 主流方法 (mainstream methods)... 近期进展 (recent advances)...\n- 一种重要的研究路径 (an important research path) / 另一种主流approach (another mainstream approach)\n- 现有研究尚存在三个开放问题 (existing research still has three open problems)\n- 笔者注意到, 现有研究普遍忽视了 X (the author notes that existing research generally overlooks X)\n\n7. CỤM IDIOMS APPLICABLE:\n\n- 开宗明义 (open with clear thesis) — for abstract first sentence\n- 言简意赅 (concise but substantive) — abstract overall\n- 一目了然 (instantly understandable) — abstract goal\n- 删繁就简 (cut redundancy) — editing process\n- 提纲挈领 (grasp the essence) — for lit review\n- 画龙点睛 (dot the dragon's eye) — for the contribution sentence\n- 画蛇添足 (add snake feet) — for unnecessary additions\n\n8. JOURNAL-SPECIFIC LIMITS:\n\n- 《文学评论》 (CASS): 200-300 words, hard limit\n- 《文学遗产》: 200-250 words\n- 《中国比较文学》: up to 350 words\n- 《古典文学研究》: 200-300 words\n- International English journals (e.g., Harvard Journal of Asiatic Studies): 150-250 words\n\nHard limit = strict. Kiểm tra journal guidelines TRƯỚC khi viết.\n\n9. BILINGUAL ABSTRACTS:\n\nTier-1 Trung Quốc journals require BOTH Chinese AND English abstract. Two abstracts must parallel ý nhưng không phải translation 1:1. Sinh viên Việt: writing two abstract bản = two job, dù share content.\n\n10. AI-ASSISTED ABSTRACT WRITING:\n\nFrom 2023+, ChatGPT/Claude widely used for drafting abstracts. Major journals require disclosure if AI was used. ACL 2024 banned AI-drafted abstracts (different from research). Sinh viên Việt: disclose any AI usage in submission letter.",
